# ── .state/.gitignore ──
# Track structure (start.md manifests), ignore accumulation.
# State is instance-specific — only the skeleton travels with the framework.

# ── ⚠ NOT A MODEL FOR CHILD PROJECTS ──
# Same inverted shape as the repo root, and for the same reason: this directory
# is framework structure holding instance-specific accumulation, so the default
# is "ignore" and only the manifests are named back in. That is a property of
# what claudette is — a framework — not a house style.
#
# A child project is insular and uses an ordinary deny-list; see
# .templates/child/.gitignore. A child's own .state/ does not need this file's
# shape, and copying it would ignore that child's content by default.

# Ignore everything
*

# Keep the directory tree walkable, so the negations below can reach their files
!*/

# ── Manifests, ANCHORED ──
# A leading slash anchors a pattern to this directory. That matters: an
# UNANCHORED `!start.md` matches at ANY depth, and both mileqa and audit runs
# stage a full copy of the codex tree under tests/<run>/ — each copy carrying
# ~30 start.md files of its own. Every one of them was being un-ignored, so
# `git add .state` would have committed a duplicate codex.
#
# Excluding the output directories instead (`tests/*/` with a `!tests/audits/`
# hole) does not hold: re-including that directory puts everything beneath it
# back under the unanchored rule, and an audit run writes its own
# `YYYYMMDD-HHMM/codex-snapshot/` inside it. Anchoring the manifests is the
# rule that cannot be re-opened by adding a directory.
#
# Adding a manifest deeper than TWO levels needs its own anchored line here.
!/.gitignore
!/start.md
!/*/start.md
# tests/ has manifests one level deeper (tests/audits/, tests/mileqa/ are both
# tracked on main); `!/tests/*/start.md` re-includes them at exactly that depth
# without re-opening the sandbox trees, which live deeper (tests/mileqa/<run>/…).
!/tests/*/start.md
# Belt-and-suspenders (from main): the anchored rule above already excludes deep
# sandbox start.md copies by depth; this names the mileqa sandbox trees explicitly.
tests/mileqa/*/sb/
